      "target_id": "IMS4-EQ4.27",
      "support_type": "computationally_supported",
      "locator": {
        "page": 66,
        "equation": "4.27"
      },
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "curator_note": "Cross-linked MØD rules. IMS_4_27_1 ([_A]1[C]2([_A]3){=}[O+.]4 >> [_A]1.[_A]3[C]2{#}[O+]4) MATCHES step_alpha_cleavage in connectivity: it cleaves R'-C (incident to the pi-forming carbon), forms the C#O(+) triple bond and quenches the O radical; CAVEAT: the departing R' is written [_A]1 without an explicit radical dot (contrast IMS_4_26_1 which writes [_A.]1) -- a cosmetic radical-marker omission, connectivity is correct. IMS_4_27_2 ([_A]1[C]2{#}[O+]3 >> [_A+]1.[C]2[O]3) cleaves the correct R-C bond and yields R(+), matching the connectivity change of step_inductive_cleavage, BUT its product CO is written with a SINGLE C-O bond ([C]2[O]3), dropping the C#O triple bond; as written it does not conserve bond order/electrons on the neutral (rather than neutral C#O). Flagged in rule_mismatches."
